1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,200
The Five-Minute Rule.

2
00:00:02,150 --> 00:00:05,125
Starting is always the hardest part.

3
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:14,537
The five-minute rule exploits a psychological quirk: committing to a dreaded task for just five minutes, with permission to stop afterward, lowers the barrier to entry.

4
00:00:14,537 --> 00:00:21,525
Most of the time, once begun, the task is not as bad as anticipated and continues beyond the five minutes.

5
00:00:21,525 --> 00:00:27,300
The rule works because anticipatory anxiety is usually worse than the experience itself.

6
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:35,412
The commitment must be genuinely small and achievable: writing one sentence, putting on running shoes, opening one textbook.

7
00:00:35,412 --> 00:00:38,662
The barrier to starting drops to nearly zero.

